{{smaller block|Out of the ''abundance'' of the heart the mouth speaketh.{{right|Mat. xii. 34.}}

The ''abundance'' [of Chaucer] is a continual fulness within the fixed limits of good taste; that of Langland is squandered in overflow.{{right|''Lowell'', Study Windows, p. 260.}}}}
