'''abusively''' (a-bū′siv-li), ''adv.'' '''1.''' In an abusive manner; rudely; reproachfully.—'''2'''†. Improperly; by misuse.
{{smaller block|Words being carelessly and ''abusively'' admitted, and as inconstantly retained. ''Glanville'', Van. of Dogmat., xvii.}}

